  "body": "<p>Yen’s directions have given <a href=\"#minerva\">Minerva</a> and <a href=\"#thorn\">Thorn</a> a person to look for: a carpet seller who may know what preceded the First Passage. After hours beside the Eternal River they gather with <a href=\"#lucido\">Lucido</a> and <a href=\"#pelegia\">Pin</a>. The others carry memories of the towers and reasons to hesitate before returning to Larkhollow. Their different journeys have left them with different pieces of the island.</p><h2 id=\"flower-the-road-around\">A road they do not all remember</h2><p>Lucido is wary of the innkeeper and the tower. Minerva asks the company to compare what they actually know before deciding to fight anything. The Child of Viota she had carried from the earlier journey has not become lasting evidence: its body is slowly vanishing.</p><p>They choose the carpet seller and follow the river. Minerva falls unusually quiet, then finds the mountain ahead with a gap in her memory. She feels as though three days passed in a second; that sensation does not establish how many days the company traveled. Thorn checks on her. Lucido wants to move away from the place where he nearly died.</p><p>Guardians watch the mountain without launching an attack. The company goes around. Lucido guides them successfully, though his own recollection briefly slips. A melody carries through the trees and petals move against the wind toward the Bell Path. Pin spots someone sitting on a carpet.</p><h2 id=\"flower-talla-in-the-alley\">Talla answers by watching the street</h2><p>Talla Briarwing greets them warmly. Thorn introduces Rose, the giant spider she has befriended, and Talla initially mistakes it for a threat. Her advice is to keep the spider out of the village for now; she mentions a recent burial and a large creature. Those remarks supply unease rather than a complete explanation of what happened.</p><p>Minerva asks for a private discussion. Talla leads them toward the market, then stops in an alley before her stall. Beyond it, merchants sell flowers, plants, keepsakes and practical goods. She keeps looking toward the corner. Minerva lowers her voice and names Yen as the person who sent them.</p><p>Asked who Viota was, Talla offers questions in verse instead of a settled history. Asked about the Keeper of What Was Once Whole, she speaks of missing days. The company has reached the person they were sent to find, but neither question has received the clear answer Minerva wanted. Lucido goes to inspect the market while Thorn keeps watch.</p><h2 id=\"flower-screams-in-the-market\">The inquiry breaks off</h2><p>Thorn and Minerva hear screams from the Petal Market. Talla warns them that going may cost them their songs. Almost at once Lucido’s message reaches Thorn: someone has been killed in a stall—the florist.</p><p>Thorn calls the news to the others and rushes toward him. Minerva readies herself and follows, frustrated that the questions have once again been interrupted. Pin rises above the alley to watch for anyone leaving quickly. Talla remains willing to talk, but the company has another immediate danger to face.</p><p>The supplied scene ends at that turn. Lucido’s report is explicit; the source does not yet show the body examined, name an attacker or explain whether the death connects to Talla’s riddles. The next journey must begin with the market, rather than an answer silently filled into its unfinished conversation.</p><p><strong>Continue reading</strong> <a href=\"#song-the-wind-cannot-finish\">Yen’s watch and the earlier search</a> · <a href=\"#larkhollow\">Larkhollow</a> · <a href=\"#verdelune\">Verdelune</a></p>",
